s, cause difficult-to-reverse errors, or require prompt escalation. Serious impact may be inferred from the described behavior even when it is not explicitly stated.\", \"examples\": \"Widespread incorrect labeling caused by conflicting instructions; required QN/safety controls being bypassed; major LT outage; systemic QA misalignment affecting a batch; Operational reports such as 'all required fields are filled but Submit stays grey' or 'the waveform loads but Play never starts' can indicate inability to complete or evaluate assigned work.\", \"signals\": [{\"index\": 0, \"text\": \"Explicit statement that assigned work cannot be completed or evaluated\"}, {\"index\": 1, \"text\": \"Safety or required QN control described as bypassed, missing, or ignored\"}, {\"index\": 2, \"text\": \"Issue reported as affecting many tasks or an entire batch\"}, {\"index\": 3, \"text\": \"Multiple distinct people or affected tasks reporting a comparable problem within the relevant project, batch, and time window, suggesting broader disruption or systemic labeling risk. Consider the number affected relative to the known active group when that information is available; do not require an explicit statement of widespread impact\"}]}, \"MEDIUM\": {\"definition\": \"Issue that may affect labeling accuracy, QA consistency, or operational efficiency, requiring clarification or intervention. Impact appears meaningful but contained or manageable based on the available context. A question alone does not establish MEDIUM, but its content may reveal consequential uncertainty.\", \"examples\": \"Recurring rubric ambiguity; conflicting QA interpretations; intermittent LT failures affecting task completion; unclear QN handling for a specific edge case. Examples include similar pairs receiving inconsistent tie judgments, reviewers disagreeing over clipping severity, or playback repeatedly failing and then recovering.\", \"signals\": [{\"index\": 0, \"text\": \"Recurring confusion about the same rul